 "text": "Hello there! How's your day treating you? Good to have you here. In simple terms, sketch is a brief idea, often funny, done quickly with few strokes, whereas study is more detailed and lifelike representation of real thing, usually for an artist to practice. Kind of. Studies give the artist skills to see, draw, and mix colours, skills that can then be used on real projects. Sounds exciting. Are you looking for one cloud to stand out, or for them all to look realistic? Which way you go away with it, sketch or study, depends on how much time you have. Sorry, I meant, which way would make you more excited? A sketch you finish tonight, or a study you improve for weeks?",
